topIssues.body:
#23953 lets `op-deployer apply` deploy OP Private private chains, which reuse their settlement chain's L1 contracts instead of deploying their own. `op-deployer prepare` refuses them for now (`checkNoPrivateChains` in `op-deployer/pkg/deployer/prepare.go`; raised in https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/pull/23953#discussion_r4488530477).

Supporting them in `prepare` means:
- in the prediction dry-run, skip the private chain and record its settlement chain's predicted (or already deployed) L1 contracts;
- leave the private chain out of the prepared deploy calldata;
- have the step that broadcasts and checks a prepared deployment accept a chain with no calldata of its own, and mark it deployed with its settlement chain;
- pin the private chain's own start block and genesis time as for any chain;
- cover adding a private chain to a settlement chain that is already deployed.

Then remove `checkNoPrivateChains`.

